WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.560
When The Twilight Saga was at its height,
it seemed like Taylor Lautner was set to become

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.270
one of Hollywood's biggest stars…but then
it didn't really turn out that way.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.990
Here's what may have happened.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.299
Faded hype

00:00:11.299 --> 00:00:15.719
Lautner's Twilight co-stars Kristen Stewart
and Robert Pattinson were clever with their

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:16.719
careers.

00:00:16.719 --> 00:00:20.520
While still attached to the franchise, they
both starred in other films, like Adventureland

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.790
and Water For Elephants.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:26.390
As a result, the duo likely had an easier
time transitioning to other roles post-Twilight.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:31.960
Lautner, however, had only a bit part in Valentine's
Day to hold him over until the franchise was

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:32.960
over.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.149
A source told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:37.300
"It's not easy to move out of the shadow of
a hit like Twilight.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.670
But he's still very young.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.989
There's time for Taylor to become more than
just Jacob."

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:43.710
Box office bomb

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:49.059
Lautner was the marquee name in 2011's Abduction,
but the movie didn't do well… at all.

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:53.640
The film was critically panned and earned
a humiliating 4 percent on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.940
That wouldn't be so bad if the box office
numbers were better, but the flick made only

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:03.229
$28 million dollars domestically, not even
breaking even on its $35 million budget.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.190
An agent told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.781
"His first movie just wasn't very good, and
it didn't justify what he was asking for at

00:01:09.781 --> 00:01:10.781
the time."

00:01:10.781 --> 00:01:13.440
"I'd be lying if I said there was no pressure
involved.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.620
But you know, I just try and stay focused
on what I can control."

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.480
Too expensive

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.210
Studios just don't think Lautner is worth
the money he asks for.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:26.230
A source told Vulture that Lautner's talent
agency...

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:30.260
"... [did] a brilliant job of convincing Hollywood
that he's the next big movie star, but didn't

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.090
convince audiences of the same."

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.990
Lautner demanded $5 million dollars for Abduction.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:40.550
When that bombed, studios could no longer
justify the $7.5 million he asked for to star

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.300
in Stretch Armstrong and the whopping $10
million to star in the re-telling of the Biblical

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.560
David and Goliath.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.740
Both movies were shelved indefinitely.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:53.430
Four years after Abduction, Tracers was Lautner's
second attempt at a leading role.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:57.640
Unfortunately, the film never even got a U.S.
theatrical release, and the reviews from those

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.190
who actually did see it were not good.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:01.900
The Ridiculous 6

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.880
Lautner seems to have gotten in tight with
Adam Sandler, landing a bit part in Grown-Ups

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.849
2 and a supporting role in the Netflix film
The Ridiculous Six.

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:15.069
Unfortunately, The Ridiculous Six not only
scored a whopping 0 percent on Rotten Tomatoes,

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:19.760
but also happened to stir up a lot of controversy
over perceived racist jokes.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.569
Lautner would probably do well to just leave
that one off of his resume.

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:25.909
Passion project

00:02:25.909 --> 00:02:30.069
In 2016, Lautner took on the film Run the
Tide, an indie drama with no budget and no

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:31.319
big studio backing.

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:35.409
It couldn't have been further from his Twilight
roots or his attempts at becoming an action

00:02:35.409 --> 00:02:36.409
hero.

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:40.780
Lautner described the film in a Metro interview
as a passion project for everyone involved.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.849
Unfortunately, reviews were dismal.

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:43.849
The A.V.

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:44.849
Club labeled it:

00:02:44.849 --> 00:02:48.340
"...bargain-basement schmaltz, too blandly
folksy even for Sundance."

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.700
...and the Young Folks claimed:

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.810
"...the emotion felt forced and it lacked
authenticity."

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:56.420
The review even zeroed in specifically on
Lautner's performance, saying that

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.540
"...he just isn't very believable, as much
as he tries to be."

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:04.209
Is it any surprise that Lautner seemed to
take a sabbatical after this?

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:05.269
Taking his time

00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:09.650
Lautner has admitted that he'll be pickier
about the roles he chooses moving forward.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:14.420
When asked by ABC News if he was worried about
being "pigeonholed" by his Twilight role,

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.420
Lautner said,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.680
"That's kind of why I want to choose things
that are different."

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:22.889
While he considers his career's direction,
Lautner's really not in any hurry to get back

00:03:22.889 --> 00:03:24.019
on a movie set.

00:03:24.019 --> 00:03:25.930
He told Reuters in November 2016,

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:30.790
"For me the biggest thing is just surrounding
myself with people that I love, just spending

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.420
time, it doesn't matter what I'm doing as
long as I'm with my friends and my family."

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.170
"When I'm not working?

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.730
You know, playing sports with my buddies.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:41.580
Watching The Bachelor."

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.180
Focused on love?

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.480
Lautner and Billie Lourd met on the set of
Scream Queens, and their onscreen romance

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.099
spilled over into real life.

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:53.680
According to People, Lourd and Lautner's rumored
relationship began in December 2016.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.769
Lourd's uncle, Todd Fisher, said the relationship
was as serious as it was adorable, telling

00:03:58.769 --> 00:03:59.769
E! News,

00:03:59.769 --> 00:04:02.099
"He's stepped up and acted like a husband
would act.

00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:06.139
Not that that's what's going on, but it's
just an amazing support system for her, and

00:04:06.139 --> 00:04:07.569
I'm glad he's in her life."

00:04:07.569 --> 00:04:11.730
However, by July 2017, Lourd and Lautner were
over as a couple.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:16.209
Is it possible that Lautner had pressed the
pause button on acting for this romance?

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:17.400
Work reunion?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:21.169
One of the brighter spots in Lautner's career
has been the gamble he took replacing Andy

00:04:21.169 --> 00:04:23.940
Samberg's character on the BBC comedy Cuckoo.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:27.590
He was playing completely against type, but
he apparently nailed it.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:29.740
According to The Telegraph, Lautner was:

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:30.840
"...very good indeed."

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:35.871
Series co-star Greg Davies also had nothing
but praise for Lautner, hinting to Metro in

00:04:35.871 --> 00:04:39.150
November 2017 that they may work together
in the future.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.150
He said,

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:41.150
"It's an unlikely friendship.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:43.030
We're doing two more series next year.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.520
I get on really well with him.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:45.770
He's a thoroughly decent chap."

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:50.050
Granted, that's not a confirmation that Lautner
is on board, but it sure seems like he's got

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.370
an open invitation and a critically-lauded
avenue to pursue should he choose to accept

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.370
it.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:56.370
Thanks for watching!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:59.000
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.430
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

